        <h3 class="mt-3 font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--color-ink)] sm:text-2xl">
          What is an SVG Optimizer and Why is It Essential for Modern Websites?
        </h3>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          <p>
            Scalable Vector Graphics (SVG) are the gold standard for icons, logos, charts, and user interface graphics. Unlike raster images (JPEG, PNG, WebP) that store static pixel grids, an SVG is an XML-based document describing 2D shapes, coordinates, curves, strokes, and colors mathematically.
          </p>
          <p>
            However, popular design suites like <strong>Figma, Adobe Illustrator, Sketch, and Inkscape</strong> are authoring tools rather than web delivery compilers. When exporting SVGs, these applications inject considerable overhead: editor namespaces, undo histories, metadata packets, nested group containers, and coordinate numbers reaching 8 or 9 decimal places. In practical terms, <strong>between 40% and 80% of an exported SVG consists of invisible bloat</strong> that browsers do not need for visual rendering.
          </p>
          <p>
            An <strong>online svg optimizer</strong> purges this unnecessary code. By parsing the underlying XML tree and simplifying geometric path data, our dedicated <strong>svg optimizer online</strong> allows developers to <strong>reduce svg file size</strong> drastically while preserving 100% visual fidelity on standard and Retina displays.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

