        </h3>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          <p>
            SVGCleanKit acts as both an automated <strong>svg cleaner</strong> and an advanced <strong>svg compressor</strong>, executing the SVGO optimization engine directly within your browser. Here is how our tool reduces payload weight:
          </p>
          
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 pt-2 md:grid-cols-2">
            <div class="rounded-[8px] border border-[var(--color-hairline)] bg-[var(--color-canvas)] p-3.5">
              <h4 class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-[var(--color-ink)]">1. Decimal Precision Truncation</h4>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-[var(--color-body)]">
                Design editors export coordinates with excessive micro-precision. Rounding path numbers to 2 or 3 decimal places immediately reduces file size by 20% to 35% without visible alteration.
              </p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="rounded-[8px] border border-[var(--color-hairline)] bg-[var(--color-canvas)] p-3.5">
              <h4 class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-[var(--color-ink)]">2. Stripping Metadata &amp; Namespaces</h4>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-[var(--color-body)]">
                Our <strong>svg cleaner</strong> purges proprietary namespaces like <code class="font-mono text-emerald-600">xmlns:inkscape</code> and <code class="font-mono text-emerald-600">xmlns:sketch</code>, along with editor comments, RDF tags, and DOCTYPE headers.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-[8px] border border-[var(--color-hairline)] bg-[var(--color-canvas)] p-3.5">
              <h4 class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-[var(--color-ink)]">3. Collapsing Empty Containers</h4>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-[var(--color-body)]">
                Nested <code class="font-mono text-emerald-600">&lt;g&gt;</code> groups created during design exploration are flattened, combining transform matrices and pruning empty nodes to lighten DOM overhead.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-[8px] border border-[var(--color-hairline)] bg-[var(--color-canvas)] p-3.5">
              <h4 class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-[var(--color-ink)]">4. Path Segment Simplification</h4>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-[var(--color-body)]">
                The <strong>svg compressor</strong> alternates between absolute (<code class="font-mono text-emerald-600">M, L</code>) and relative (<code class="font-mono text-emerald-600">m, l</code>) commands based on which consumes fewer bytes, consolidating straight-line runs.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-[8px] border border-[var(--color-hairline)] bg-[var(--color-canvas)] p-3.5">
              <h4 class="font-sans text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-[var(--color-ink)]">5. Color Notation Minification</h4>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-[var(--color-body)]">
                Verbose colors such as <code class="font-mono text-emerald-600">#ffffff</code> are compressed to their 3-digit shorthand <code class="font-mono text-emerald-600">#fff</code>, and presentation attributes are normalized for CSS theming.
              </p>
