        <h3 class="mt-3 font-sans text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--color-ink)] sm:text-2xl">
          Vector Optimization Best Practices for Designers and Web Developers
        </h3>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          <p>
            To achieve maximum compression ratios when using an <strong>svg optimizer online</strong>, integrate these vector design habits into your workflow:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>
              <strong>Unify Vector Shapes:</strong> Combine overlapping paths with Pathfinder or Boolean Union operations before exporting from Figma or Illustrator to eliminate hidden path segments.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Convert Text to Outlines:</strong> Outline fonts to avoid layout rendering anomalies if external web fonts fail to load.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Adopt Consistent ViewBoxes:</strong> Standardize on an explicit <code class="font-mono text-xs">viewBox</code> attribute (e.g. <code class="font-mono text-xs">0 0 24 24</code>) rather than fixed pixel dimensions for responsive sizing.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Maintain 2 or 3 Decimal Precision:</strong> For standard icons and logos, 2 or 3 decimals deliver sub-pixel precision while cutting file weight. Higher precision is only necessary for intricate scientific charts.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Clean Icons Before Git Commits:</strong> Run assets through SVGCleanKit before committing to your repository to keep codebases lean and maintain clean diffs.
            </li>
          </ul>
